=== PROPOSAL ===
  action      : rollback_image (rollback)
  target      : ad
  expect      : Ad's log stream, silent since the 11:34:37 shutdown-hook line, resumes with a gRPC server-started entry and AdService request lines; frontend's repeating 'UNAVAILABLE ... EHOSTUNREACH 172.18.0.19:9555' lines stop within ~60s of ad listening; sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name="ad"}[5m])) returns non-zero samples instead of none.
  within      : 300s
  risk        : If the diagnosis is wrong, this forces another restart on a service that may already be recovering on a later flap cycle, dropping its in-process cache and any in-flight ad requests. If the recorded prior reference is 'unset', the recreate may leave ad with no runnable image, turning an intermittent outage into a continuous one. It does not address the flapping automation, so relief may be temporary and may mask the real fault.
  blast radius: One service, ad. Frontend sees connections reset during the recreate; it is already failing every call to this endpoint, so the marginal harm is small. Checkout, product-catalog, recommendation, cart, product-reviews and frontend-proxy share the blast radius and would notice only if they also call ad.
  if wrong    : Falsified if ad logs show a started server but frontend still emits EHOSTUNREACH to 172.18.0.19:9555 (the IP-to-ad mapping is topology inference, never confirmed). Also falsified if ad is stopped again within ~13 minutes: platform-automation flapped the image nine times on an 11-13 minute cycle, so the controller, not the artifact, is the fault, and stopping it is outside this system's reach. Third falsifier: no concrete prior tag exists (reverts return to unset) and the recreate fails to start.
  rests on    : tr_01c07e0c0e82, tr_c85bcff4e31a, tr_6ff7346a746a
  execution   : not executed - a proposal is a claim, never the change (ADR-0028 §1)

context: 25595 pushed / 4637 pulled (pull rate 0.1534), 2 section(s) dropped

=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : bad_deploy
  fix class   : rollback
  confidence  : medium
  evidence    : tr_6ff7346a746a, tr_c85bcff4e31a, tr_01c07e0c0e82, tr_0f07ecb071ff, tr_a2f0a0ac1ded
  root cause  : Frontend's failures are entirely transport-level gRPC UNAVAILABLE connect errors (EHOSTUNREACH) to a single upstream endpoint 172.18.0.19:9555, with no connection ever established [tr_6ff7346a746a]. That endpoint is the ad service, whose log stream ends at 11:34:37 with an orderly JVM-shutdown-hook gRPC server stop after serving traffic cleanly, and emits nothing thereafter [tr_c85bcff4e31a]. The cause of the absence is in ad's change log: platform-automation flapped ad's image reference nine times in two hours, alternating set-to-hotfix-tag and revert-to-unset on an 11-13 minute cycle, with a set landing at 11:34:38, one second after the shutdown [tr_01c07e0c0e82]. The running artifact for ad is therefore not a correct, stable one, and during the gaps nothing listens on 9555, so callers get host-unreachable. Frontend is the reporter, not the fault: no changes [tr_a2f0a0ac1ded] and an error-span ratio below baseline with no step change at onset [tr_0f07ecb071ff].
  OPEN        : The ad/172.18.0.19:9555 mapping is topology inference, not evidence; no result ties that IP to an ad pod [tr_6ff7346a746a].
  OPEN        : The ad error-ratio query covered 2026-10-05, a day before the incident [tr_0361fa04f99c], so its 100%-error baseline and empty window may describe a different period.
  OPEN        : Why platform-automation is flapping the image reference, and whether ad recovered on a later cycle, is unestablished; six of eight blast-radius services were never queried.

