=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : network_partition
  fix class   : reconnect
  confidence  : medium
  evidence    : tr_2fb5ffc9c7e7, tr_472153e4ed14, tr_751b4dbe028b
  root cause  : Frontend fails ~3.4% of calls (peak 8.4%) because one gRPC upstream at 172.18.0.19:9555 is unreachable at the network layer. Frontend's log shows only gRPC status-14 UNAVAILABLE with underlying TCP EHOSTUNREACH against that single address, continuously from 11:39:33 through 12:11:13 and with a connect attempt at 12:09:36 right on the alert time [tr_2fb5ffc9c7e7]. EHOSTUNREACH is no-route-to-host, not a refusal or a timeout, so the mechanism is lost reachability to that endpoint rather than anything frontend computes wrong. Frontend's other downstreams still answer in the same traces [tr_751b4dbe028b], so frontend is not cut off generally — only from that one peer, which in this deployment is the ad service's gRPC port. No deploy, config edit, or flag flip appears for frontend or any downstream in the preceding 24h [tr_02526dd4aae4], consistent with a connectivity loss rather than a change.
  OPEN        : No dispatch resolved 172.18.0.19:9555 to a named service; the attribution to ad is inferred from the standard gRPC port and from ad spans appearing in traces, not confirmed by evidence.
  OPEN        : No specialist examined ad directly — its own logs would distinguish a partition (ad running and complaining) from a crashed or descheduled pod (silence plus an IP that no longer routes).
  OPEN        : The 30-minute-wide trace-level slowness in product-reviews (get_ai_assistant_response at 74% of trace time) is unexplained and may be an independent concurrent issue rather than a consequence of the unreachable peer.

