  action      : rollback_image (rollback)
  target      : ad
  expect      : ad logs resume (gRPC ads server startup, then routine request lines), ending the silence that began at the 12:25:29 shutdown-hook teardown; frontend stops logging status 14 UNAVAILABLE / host-unreachable to 172.18.0.19:9555, and the frontend and frontend-proxy alerts clear. The effect comes mainly from the container recreate, not the tag value — the same tag ran healthily earlier in the week. Confirmation must be from Loki on both sides: ad metrics are unusable here (both Prometheus queries returned HTTP 400).
  within      : 300s
  risk        : If the real defect is the automation leaving zero replicas rather than the image, this restores service only until the next apply/revert cycle (~10-20 min) and masks the loop. The recreate itself discards ad's in-process cache and briefly resets any connection that had recovered.
