  root cause  : The ad service stopped existing on the network at 12:25:29 and did not return. Its own log shows clean traffic up to the final second, then an orderly JVM shutdown-hook teardown of the gRPC ads server and total silence afterwards [tr_fb2d7b15b665]; one second later the change log records platform-automation setting ad's image reference from unset to the 2.2.0-ad-hotfix.2 tag [tr_2ab1b562f262]. From 12:30 the frontend logs gRPC status 14 UNAVAILABLE against one peer, 172.18.0.19:9555 (the conventional ad port), with a host-unreachable connect error — no TCP session is ever established, so the peer is absent rather than refusing or hanging [tr_fe847d5db367]. The deploy action terminated the running replica and no healthy replacement came up on that address: the artifact that should be running is not running. The frontend and frontend-proxy alerts are caller-side propagation of the missing dependency.
  OPEN        : Did a replacement ad pod ever start — crashlooping, stuck pulling the hotfix tag, or never scheduled? No availability or restart metric was retrieved; both queries failed with HTTP 400 [tr_361e4ee9a7d6].
  OPEN        : The frontend log names only 172.18.0.19:9555, not a service name; ad attribution rests on port convention plus the coincident shutdown [tr_fe847d5db367].
